pydebuprep (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New checks:
    - network: default route and DNS; with a baseline, interfaces, addresses,
      routes, DNS and the network manager.
    - firewall: ufw or nftables enabled but no rules loaded; rules lost since
      the baseline.
    - time-sync: a time service runs and the clock is synchronised.
    - apparmor: disabled, complain-mode profiles, denials, lost enforcement.
    - unattended-upgrades: disabled, or origins naming the old release.
    - cron: jobs whose program no longer exists; no cron daemon.
    - ssh-server: sshd -t errors and warnings; DSA keys in authorized_keys.
    - postgresql, mariadb, postfix, bind, docker and python-venvs, in a new
      applications section.
  * boot-time shows the critical chain; disk-space has a minimum free space
    for / and /var (important_mounts, min_free_mib).
  * Snapshots are private: the directory is 0700 and each file 0600.
    Upgrading tightens /var/lib/pydebuprep from 0750. (CodeQL
    py/overly-permissive-file)
  * New options: config-conflicts.ignore_paths for files a configuration tool
    manages, and a shared 'logs: ignore:' list of regular expressions for
    journal-errors and dmesg-errors.
  * Without a baseline, the report says so once instead of in every check.
  * fstab: swap files are no longer reported when the fstab target is 'swap'.
  * Runs without python3-yaml when YAML isn't needed, with an install hint
    when it is.
  * Documentation: SECURITY.md, a CHECKS section in the man page, README
    badges and install instructions for GitHub releases.

 -- Jostein Elvaker Haande <jehaande@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:25:39 +0100

pydebuprep (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Configuration file /etc/pydebuprep.conf (YAML) with per-check options,
    plus configtest and example-config commands and --check-option.
  * New output formats: jira and confluence (wiki markup).
  * disk-space checks local filesystems only unless include_remote is set.
  * Snapshots record enabled as well as active services.
  * Output directory is validated before checks run; baseline host and
    release mismatches are warned about even when os-release is skipped.
  * bash and zsh completion, generated from the command-line parser and
    installed for both shells.
  * apt-mark now runs with the same read-only options as apt; as root it
    could rebuild /var/cache/apt/pkgcache.bin.
  * Regular-expression options keep commas; '-o -' writes to standard
    output even when the configuration sets output_dir; stricter config
    validation.
  * Jira/Confluence escaping covers list, strikethrough and icon markup.
  * Relative paths in the configuration file resolve against its directory.
  * Every release is built once and audited with strace on Debian 12, 13
    and Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04 and 26.04 to prove a run changes nothing.

 -- Jostein Elvaker Haande <jehaande@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:20:50 +0100

